  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` now passes with 6 of 6 tests.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never freed its slot, so the queue stalled. Now a job's slot is released whether it resolves or rejects. Jobs that throw synchronously or return a plain value are handled too, and each only rejects or resolves its own promise.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving too early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits until nothing is running.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `resume()` started a single job. It now keeps starting jobs until every free slot is filled, and the same loop runs when a job finishes.\n\nI added four regression tests in `test/queue.test.js`:\n- The queue keeps going after a rejected job and after a synchronous throw.\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs.\n- `onIdle()` resolves immediately when the queue is already idle.\n- `resume()` fills all four slots at concurrency 4.",
